## Task 1 - Create a Domain

A Domain is based on a Governed Tag. When you create a Domain, a Governed Tag with the same name is created automatically.

1. Click **Discover** in the left sidebar, then click **Create** → **Create domain** in the top right.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-04-create-domain.png', 'Discover > Create domain') }}

2. Leave **Source** as **New tag**, and enter `{{ cat }}` (e.g., `{{ ex_cat }}`) in the input field on the right. Fill in the other fields as shown below, then click **Create**.

    | Field | Value |
    |---|---|
    | **Subtitle** | `{{ s.domain.subtitle }}` |
    | **Description** | `{{ s.domain.description }}` |
    | **Business Contacts** (optional) | Yourself |

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-06-domain-form.png', 'Enter Domain information') }}

3. The Domain is created in **Draft** status. Click **Publish** in the top right to make it visible to other users.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-07-publish-domain.png', 'Publish Domain') }}

## Task 2 - Link Tags to Metric Views

1. In **Catalog**, navigate to `{{ cat }}` → `default` → `{{ mv1.name }}`.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-08-open-mv-1.png', 'Open ' ~ mv1.name) }}

2. Scroll down to the **About this metric view** section, and click **Add tags** under **Tags**.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-09-add-tags.png', 'Add tags') }}

3. Type in **Key** to find and select `{{ cat }}`, leave **Value** empty, and click **Save**.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-10-select-tag-save.png', 'Select tag and save') }}

4. Repeat the same process to link the tag to `{{ mv2.name }}`.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-11-tag-mv-2.png', 'Link tag to ' ~ mv2.name) }}

??? tip "Link Tags with SQL"
    You can also link tags by running these queries in SQL Editor:

    ```sql
    ALTER VIEW {{ cat }}.default.{{ mv1.name }}
      SET TAGS ('{{ cat }}' = '');
    ALTER VIEW {{ cat }}.default.{{ mv2.name }}
      SET TAGS ('{{ cat }}' = '');
    ```

## Task 3 - Verify in the Domain

1. Click **Discover** in the left sidebar, then click **Domain** in the filter bar at the top. Search for your name and select `{{ cat }}`.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-12-open-domain.png', 'Select Domain') }}

2. Verify that `{{ mv1.name }}` and `{{ mv2.name }}` appear on the Domain page.

    {{ shot('03-uc-semantics/3-3-13-domain-assets.png', 'Metric Views linked to Domain') }}

!!! info "Tags may take a few minutes to appear"
    It may take a few minutes for linked assets to show up on the Domain page. If you don't see them immediately, refresh after a moment.

!!! success "Congratulations!"
    You've completed {{ da.name | poss }} work. You've defined business KPIs as Metric Views and organized {{ s.domain.assets_noun }} into a Domain. Next, in Step 4, you'll become {{ ai.title }} {{ ai.name }} and build a Genie Agent using these Metric Views for {{ bu.title }} {{ bu.name }}.
